BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Monthly Introduction to Solutions Journalism Webinar: May
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260505T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260505T000000
UID:622652596192812bc228c7cbbd8426d6@solutionsjournalism.org
DESCRIPTION:Online (Zoom)\nThis one-hour Solutions Journalism Network webi
 nar will explore the principles and pillars of solutions journalism. We wi
 ll discuss its importance\, outline key steps for reporting a solutions st
 ory\, and share tips and resources for journalists investigating responses
  to social problems. We will also introduce additional resources\, such as
  the Solutions Story Tracker\, a database with over 17\,000 stories tagged
  by beat\, publication\, author\, location and more\, along with a virtual
  heat map highlighting successful efforts worldwide.
LOCATION:Online (Zoom)
URL:https://us06web.zoom.us/webinar/register/WN_9ykIGH3URYCXHGW7e5cmng
X-SOURCE:Solutions Journalism Network
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Find Your People: Engagement Strategies for Bringing Solutions Rep
 orting to the Community
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260507T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260507T000000
UID:12aba9a42d7aef26944e00cf3fbeeb0a@solutionsjournalism.org
DESCRIPTION:Online\nThere is sometimes a gulf in reporting: Whether due to
  trust or access\, the people most in need of the information can struggle
  to obtain it. SomeAdvancing Democracy granteeshave been addressing that i
 n creative ways. You can learn from them at “Find your people: Engagemen
 t strategies for bringing solutions reporting to the community.”\nWe’v
 e got two sessions\, May 7 and May 21\, each featuring two different newsr
 ooms finding success with including the public in solutions journalism. An
 d we’ll help you build your own road map for meaningful engagement — n
 ot just adding to your reach\, but building real relationships. You can si
 gn up for one or both.\nPart one — May 7: Gulf States Newsroom and Factc
 hequeado share how they embedded community listening into their solutions 
 reporting for the first time.\nPart two — May 21: Crosswinds News and Te
 xas Standard discuss building on prior solutions journalism training to de
 epen engagement on Native inclusion and adult education beats.
LOCATION:Online
URL:https://us06web.zoom.us/meeting/register/5-jrs4mPSyezTFfrCwoPdw?mc_cid
 =9d4c8b8c83&mc_eid=f6b9d64e2d#/registration
X-SOURCE:Solutions Journalism Network
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Climate Peer Network Meeting
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260514T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260514T000000
UID:efd5730096f0797d20ebad52453895f2@solutionsjournalism.org
DESCRIPTION:Online (Zoom)\nJoin the next meeting of our Climate Peer Netwo
 rk! It’s a space for solutions-minded climate journalists from around th
 e world to connect\, brainstorm and tap into the wisdom of the network.Joi
 n up to attend the May 14 gathering (or subsequent ones).
